  <section>
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>The Healing Community MEDCo is a Maine medical cannabis dispensary operating from a downtown Gardiner storefront at 189 Water Street. Per the operator's own marketing (via Leafly), MEDCo offers "the most extensive line of top-shelf medical cannabis and cannabis products in the state of Maine" in a "laid back, leisurely shopping experience."</p>
    <p>MEDCo is one of at least five medical dispensaries operating in the small town of Gardiner — an unusually high density for a town of fewer than 6,000 residents. The Kennebec River corridor between Gardiner and Augusta has become a regional medical cannabis hub, with multiple operators clustered along the river.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Downtown Gardiner Location</h2>
    <p><strong>Address:</strong> 189 Water Street, Gardiner, ME 04345</p>
    <p>Water Street is the main commercial corridor in downtown Gardiner, running along the west bank of the Kennebec River. The dispensary sits in the historic downtown commercial district, with restaurants, retail, and other small businesses in the surrounding blocks. Parking is available on the street and in nearby public lots. The storefront is a short walk from the city's landmark downtown bridge across the Kennebec.</p>
    <p>Confirm current hours directly with the operator before visiting. Per the public Loc8NearMe and MapQuest listings, the storefront operates on a standard medical dispensary schedule — call or check the online menu for the most current hours.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Product Menu</h2>
    <p>Per the operator's own site and the Weedmaps listing, MEDCo carries a full Maine medical dispensary menu:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Flower</strong> — multiple cultivars, indoor and outdoor</li>
      <li><strong>Pre-rolls</strong> — single joints, multi-packs, and house blend prerolls (a customer-favorite per the Weedmaps reviews)</li>
      <li><strong>Cartridges / Vapes</strong> — 510-thread carts and disposables</li>
      <li><strong>Concentrates</strong> — solvent and solventless extracts including shatter (per reviews)</li>
      <li><strong>Edibles</strong> — gummies, chocolates, and "medicated wholefoods" (per the operator's site)</li>
      <li><strong>Tinctures</strong> — sublingual and oral formats</li>
      <li><strong>Beverages</strong> — infused drinks</li>
      <li><strong>Topicals / Salves</strong> — non-inhalable medical formats</li>
      <li><strong>CBD products</strong> — broad-spectrum and isolate formats</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The "medicated wholefoods" framing on the operator's site suggests a focus on artisanal, made-in-Maine edible products rather than just gummies and chocolates. Confirm current inventory directly with the operator.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Kennebec Valley Service Area</h2>
    <p>MEDCo's downtown Gardiner location serves the Kennebec River corridor:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Gardiner</strong> (in town) — 5 min</li>
      <li><strong>Hallowell</strong> — 5-10 min north</li>
      <li><strong>Randolph</strong> — 10 min north</li>
      <li><strong>Farmingdale</strong> — 10 min north</li>
      <li><strong>Pittston</strong> — 10 min east</li>
      <li><strong>West Gardiner</strong> — 10 min west</li>
      <li><strong>Augusta</strong> (state capital, across the river) — 10-15 min south</li>
      <li><strong>Richmond</strong> — 20 min south</li>
      <li><strong>Litchfield / Wales</strong> — 20-30 min southwest</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Augusta residents (the state capital, with a population of ~19,000 in the greater metro) find MEDCo a convenient medical dispensary option across the river. The Kennebec Valley medical patient base is well-served by the cluster of dispensaries in and around Gardiner.</p>
  </section>

